course: dictionary
lesson: 7916
title: Ravines: deep valleys cut by water
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A ravine is a deep, narrow valley with steep sides. Picture a crack in the land, with a stream or river running along the bottom.
explain: Ravines form slowly. Water keeps running over the rock for a very long time and cuts deeper and deeper into the ground. The words around ravine give you clues: «a deep ravine» and «the bottom of the ravine» tell you it is a hollow, not a hill.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence. «At Babyn Yar, a ravine in Kyiv» makes sense if ravine means a deep, narrow valley. It does.
fact: A ravine is a deep, narrow valley with steep sides.
fact: Ravines are usually cut by a stream or river over a long time.
fact: Useful phrases: «a deep ravine», «the bottom of the ravine», «cross the ravine».
fact: In stories, heroes sometimes cross a ravine on a rope bridge.
fact: Babyn Yar is a ravine in Kyiv, and today people come there quietly to remember.
exercise: «We walked along the bottom of the ravine, where the stream ran over the stones.» What is a ravine? | *A deep, narrow valley with steep sides | A small pond in a field | A tall, flat hill with a wide top | A road cut through a town
exercise: How was most of a ravine made? | Quickly, in one afternoon by builders | *Slowly, by a stream or river cutting into the rock over a long time | By snow falling in one night | By people digging for gold in a single day
exercise: In «a deep ravine», which word tells you how far down it goes? | a | the | ravine | *deep
test: What is a ravine? | A flat, sandy beach | A tall tower of stone | A hot desert | *A deep, narrow valley with steep sides
test: In stories, what do heroes sometimes do at a ravine? | Sleep in it all winter | Build a castle on top of it | Count the stars above it | *Cross it on a rope bridge
exam: Which sentence uses ravine correctly? | *The stream had cut a deep ravine through the rock over many years | A ravine is a small, round puddle left after rain | Ravines are usually flat and sandy | Builders make ravines in one afternoon
